OrionLayer open fix 68 — the battle's OPTIONS panel on the wire
================================================================

Work order 200 (Part A, step A2). orion2re 095ebac4 on `orionlayer-local`,
on top of a8381e60 (open fix 67). src/ext only.

WHAT IS MISSING. OPTIONS (the battle panel's info button, hotkey O) flips
MOX::_order_info_flag and slides COMBAT.LBX 9 up over the buttons
(Move_Options_Background_, cmbtdrw1.cpp:1463); its five lights are MOX's
flags for the missile warning, fast animations, legal moves, shield arcs
and the grid (Draw_Option_Panel_Lights_, cmbtdrw1.cpp:1307-1322), toggled
by five hidden fields (combat1.cpp:465-495). The flags are copied from
_settings when a battle starts (combinit.cpp:529-534) and written back only
when it ends (combinit.cpp:1177-1178), so the settings record on the wire
is stale for the whole battle; whether the panel is up was not on the wire
at all. A client could neither show the panel nor its lights, nor draw the
grid, the shield arcs or the legal moves as the battle holds them.

WHAT THE PATCH ADDS. Snapshot section 26, "COPT", after CPOP, written only
while a battle is live: a version byte, int16 the battle's serial and
MOX::_order_info_flag (0 while the panel is up), then five bytes — the
missile warning, fast animations, legal moves, shield arcs and grid flags,
the panel's lights in its own order.

BEHAVIOUR WITHOUT ORIONLAYER: unchanged. The block is read only; nothing
in the game changes.

HOW TO REVERT. git revert 095ebac4.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index aa70fced..0d840a43 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -1760,6 +1760,34 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
         Write8(buf, (uint8_t)len);
         buf.insert(buf.end(), msg, msg + len);
     }
+
+    // 26. The battle's OPTIONS panel: "COPT", written ONLY while a battle is
+    //     live, after CPOP. OrionLayer, open fix 68.
+    //
+    //     OPTIONS (the info button, hotkey O) flips MOX::_order_info_flag and
+    //     slides COMBAT.LBX 9 over the buttons (Move_Options_Background_,
+    //     cmbtdrw1.cpp:1463); its five lights are MOX's flags for the missile
+    //     warning, fast animations, legal moves, shield arcs and the grid
+    //     (Draw_Option_Panel_Lights_, :1307-1322), toggled by five hidden
+    //     fields (combat1.cpp:465-495). The flags are copied from _settings
+    //     when the battle starts (combinit.cpp:529-534) and back only when
+    //     it ends (:1177-1178), so the settings record on the wire is stale
+    //     for the whole battle, and neither the panel nor the flags were on
+    //     the wire. Read only; nothing here changes the game.
+    if (g_combat_live && MOX::_combat_data != nullptr) {
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'C');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'O');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'P');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'T');
+        Write8(buf, 1);                                   // block version
+        Write16(buf, (int16_t)g_combat_serial);
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_order_info_flag);              // 0: the panel is up
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::_msl_impact_warning_flag);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::_speedx2_flag);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::_draw_legal_boxes_flag);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::_shields_flag);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::_grid_flag);
+    }
 }
 
